      <memberdef kind="function" id="_marmot_wiechert_8h_1a31e07d2c5576be3efa1ed7a4233b4f9c" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <templateparamlist>
          <param>
            <type>int</type>
            <declname>k</declname>
            <defname>k</defname>
          </param>
        </templateparamlist>
        <type>Properties</type>
        <definition>Properties Marmot::ContinuumMechanics::Viscoelasticity::Wiechert::computeElasticModuli</definition>
        <argsstring>(std::function&lt; autodiff::Real&lt; k, double &gt;(autodiff::Real&lt; k, double &gt;) &gt; psi, const Properties &amp;relaxationTimes, double spacing, bool gaussQuadrature=false)</argsstring>
        <name>computeElasticModuli</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::ContinuumMechanics::Viscoelasticity::Wiechert::computeElasticModuli</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>std::function&lt; autodiff::Real&lt; k, double &gt;(autodiff::Real&lt; k, double &gt;) &gt;</type>
          <declname>psi</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const Properties &amp;</type>
          <declname>relaxationTimes</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>double</type>
          <declname>spacing</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>bool</type>
          <declname>gaussQuadrature</declname>
          <defval>false</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute the elastic moduli of the Maxwell units of a Wiechert chain. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The relaxation spectrum is integrated over the logarithmic relaxation-time axis, which is discretized by the relaxation times with the given spacing. By default a one-point rule is used, i.e. the modulus of the unit with relaxation time <formula id="3">$\tau_i$</formula> is <formula id="4">$\ln(\mathrm{spacing}) \, S(\tau_i)$</formula>, where <formula id="5">$S$</formula> is the relaxation spectrum. With Gauss quadrature the two-point Gauss rule over the logarithmic interval of the unit is used.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>k</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>order of the Post-Widder approximation of the relaxation spectrum </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">psi</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>relaxation function </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">relaxationTimes</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>relaxation times of the Maxwell units </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">spacing</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>ratio of two consecutive relaxation times </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">gaussQuadrature</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>use the two-point Gauss rule instead of the one-point rule </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>the elastic moduli, one per Maxwell unit </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
